      "why": "Kept only as cheap insurance: for identical (W, N, angle_guard, frac_guard, rounding) it computes the same bits as iterative but needs k chained micro-rotations per cycle, so it cannot be on the area-accuracy front unless something unexpected happens at small k. Ranges are deliberately narrow (low/mid W, k 2-4) so the few evals probe the only place it could conceivably compete - the low-area corner - rather than wasting budget on the high-accuracy end where it is clearly dominated.",
      "ranges": [
