{
  "decision": "stop",
  "rationale": "This is the final round, and the front is both feasible and well-covered, so stopping is correct. Constraints are satisfied with margin: 0% of evaluations violate throughput_msps >= 1 (best seen 36.5 MSPS, and every front design is 4.56-11.7 MSPS), and the accuracy constraint max_abs_err <= 2^-10 is met by all 27 front designs (worst front point 2^-11.27, best 2^-24.11). The front spans luts_plus_ffs 278..625 against the HV reference 1500 and accuracy_bits 11.3..24.1 against the HV reference 10, i.e. it already covers the trade-off curve well past both reference points (HV 1.482e+04, +26.5% this round). The selection rule (min luts_plus_ffs) picks the iterative [data_width=15 n_iter=14 angle_guard=2 frac_guard=2 rounding=trunc] design at luts_plus_ffs=278, accuracy_bits=11.3, throughput 11.7 MSPS - comfortably inside both constraints. No constraint is unreachable, so infeasible is not warranted; further refinement is not possible in the remaining budget."
  ,
